VirtConvert
===========

VirtConvert is an independent project. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by or sponsored by
Microsoft (Hyper-V, Azure), Oracle (VirtualBox) or Broadcom/VMware; those names appear only to
describe the disk image formats VirtConvert works with.

Tools it runs (not bundled)
---------------------------

* qemu-img from the QEMU project, GPL-2.0-or-later, https://www.qemu.org — writes the converted
  disk images and compares them with their sources.

VirtConvert reads VHD, VHDX and VDI headers and differencing images itself, following the
published specifications (Microsoft "Virtual Hard Disk Image Format Specification" and
[MS-VHDX], and VirtualBox's VDI layout).

The design system of the app (theme.py, icons.py, worker.py and parts of widgets.py) is shared
with EZP2019Linux, DiskHealth, CloneAndRecover and the other applications by the same author.
